            <ArticleTitle>Striae: a potential precipitating factor for Koebner phenomenon in psoriasis?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>18186</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Koebner phenomenon (isomorphic response) is defined as the development of typical lesions of a dermatosis that occur in areas of trauma in previously uninvolved skin. Rare reports have suggested that striae are a form of injury to the skin that can result in koebnerization of psoriasis, vitiligo, and lichen planus. We herein report a 27-year-old female patient with plaque psoriasis who developed psoriatic lesions along striae distensae.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
